What is the output of the following Java program calling an overridden method through a superclass reference?
```java
class CanvasLayer {
    public String describe() {
        return "BaseLayer";
    }
}
class VectorLayer extends CanvasLayer {
    @Override
    public String describe() {
        return "VectorLayer:" + super.describe();
    }
}
public class LayerDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CanvasLayer layer = new VectorLayer();
        System.out.println(layer.describe());
    }
}
```

